<!--
    REA fork: iOS 27 dark key.

    The design's key is a flat translucent fill (border-radius 9px on a 43px key); the
    ramp belongs to the panel, not to the keys. The radius below is the one the theme
    actually draws with (Ios27Palette.KEY_RADIUS_DP), which the hairline of the soft
    shading is cut to as well, so the two have to stay in step. Colors tints this white
    with the theme key colour in MODULATE mode, so a flat white here is what makes the
    key read as one uniform surface instead of the top-lit bevel this fork started with.

    The design's inset top highlight (inset 0 1px 0 #ffffff25) is deliberately absent:
    MODULATE can only darken, so a highlight baked in as white would render as the
    key colour itself and be invisible. It is drawn as a separate untinted hairline
    instead; see SurfaceShading.keyShading.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
       android:shape="rectangle">
    <corners android:radius="7dp" />
    <solid android:color="@android:color/white" />
</shape>
